  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   The proposed approach combines several optimizations: multi-resolution analysis, advanced optimization algorithms, and innovative search accelerators. Unlike the parent algorithm which uses black-box random exploration, our method leverages gradient information and introduces correlates between phase space elements. This tackles the non-convex optimization head-on by maintaining a dual search landscape and dynamically adjusting objectives based on perceived obstacles. The key innovation is the specialized phase genotype separators that reduce dimensionality during critical transitions and the periodic surrogate validation.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   - Representation: piecewise-constant step function with unit integral constraint\n   - Objective: minimize C\u2085 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n   - Constraint: \u222b h(x)dx = 1, 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1\n   - Hyperparameters: dynamic alpha in simplex triplets, periodically updated smoothing factor\n   - Algorithms: hybrid Grippo-Lampariello-Th-Based exploration with coupling between gradient and derivative-free regions\n   - Dimensionality reduction via:  \n     \u2022 Active relevance filtering: hinders redundant evaluation points  \n     \u2022 Lag distribution: restricted convolution patterns\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   - Prepare input array (initial\u2264560 samples)\n   - Phase initialization: organized RachelProjection()\n   - Optimization\u00f7Decomposition:\n     1. Create k\u2208[0, n-1] simplex sampling of hypercube {0,1}\n     2. Use phase separation to assign functionality via:\n        - Linear/constraint phase\n        - Objective extraction with penalty parameters\n        - Cache growth metric\n     3. Call simplex method until target value C<0.3808\n   - Valid/Invalid checks via adapted fitness projection\n   - Phase termination window: 60 seconds per core\n   - Dynamic reconfiguration if failure detected\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n   - Base configuration: initial flagged phase weights; fallback seedings\n   - Alternate variations:\n     - Phase equality checks at 0.01 C5threshold\n     - Directional correction factor for gradient components\n     - Active selection: scores/inheritance\n   - Standard deviations: \u00b115% from base timeout metrics\n\n5. Budget and robustness\n   - Dominant cost: dNCH\u7fb9 = n \u00d7 T_{sa} + l \u00d7 T_{adam} (seconds)\n   - Acceptance criteria: crossing thresholds triggers fallback\n   - Internal clock monitoring: early detection\n   - Fallback: ranked reserves\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - Final result passed to Erd\u0151s evaluator\n   - Fish dependency: none\n   - Meticulous recalibration at each prod point\n   - \u0422et licensee: th\u01b0\u00f9ng, clear boundaries",
